WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.760
- [Narrator] The rocky inner
planets of our solar system

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.340
are thought to have mostly metallic cores,

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.800
a building block of planet formation.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.560
But because the cores are
so difficult to reach,

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.950
scientists can only speculate
on their exact composition,

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.720
and what stories they might tell us

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.910
about the origins of our planets,

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.533
But that's about to change.

00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:22.533
(rocket taking off)

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.870
- [NASA Employee] Vehicles
pitching down range.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.060
- This is the first time
NASA has ever sent a mission

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.670
to this type of world,
a mostly metal world.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.200
- [Narrator] Here's a
look at a NASA mission

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.640
to the asteroid, Psyche.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.710
What scientists think is a metallic core

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.450
from a planet that never formed

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.160
and how the mission could tell us more

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.023
about the origins of planet Earth.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.290
More than 1 million asteroids
have been discovered

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.760
in our solar system.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.090
Of those millions, Psyche was
the 16th to be discovered,

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.640
dating back to the mid-1800s.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.160
Most asteroids are made of rock and ice,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.410
but scientists believe
the Psyche asteroid,

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.830
named after the greek goddess
of the soul, is made of metal.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.660
- In the earliest days
of our solar system,

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.820
about 4.5 billion years ago,

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.130
there were a lot of objects made of metal

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.550
and rock and ice that were
violently colliding together,

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.340
some of them accreted to form the cores

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.700
and outer layers of our
planets like Earth and Mars.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.620
The best theory so far is that Psyche

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:26.400
is one of the sort of exposed
cores of these planetesimals,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.010
these planets that never came to be.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.630
- [Narrator] But until
the Psyche spacecraft

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.120
arrives at the asteroid in 2029,

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.920
scientists can't say for certain

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.470
that this is Psyche's origin story.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.230
- [Aylin] Even though we don't
know its origin and genesis

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.460
with complete certainty,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.300
the value of a mission
like this is unprecedented.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.950
- [Narrator] A recent analysis by NASA

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.960
indicates that Psyche is likely made

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.910
of a mixture of rock and metal,

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:55.470
with metal composing between
30-60% of its volume.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.120
But why are scientists spending

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.720
more than $1 billion to study metal?

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.140
- The fact that it's
possibly the exposed core

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.600
of one of these
protoplanets is significant,

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.390
because Earth formed from the accretion

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.550
of many, many protoplanets.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:14.580
And so Psyche is one small microcosm

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:18.600
of a building block of what
came to make Earth, Earth.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:19.800
- [Narrator] Earth's outer core

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.620
lies at a depth of over 1,800 miles.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.020
So far, scientists have only drilled down

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.240
about seven and a half of those miles,

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.510
because that's as far as our
current technology can take us.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.220
- And because we can't travel back in time

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.260
to the earliest days of our solar system

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.360
and we can't right now delve into

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.130
the center of our own planet,

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:40.620
Psyche provides this excellent proxy

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.440
for trying to better
understand the evolution

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.180
of our planetary neighborhood.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.160
- [Narrator] To study the
asteroids composition,

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.190
the Psyche spacecraft,
made by Maxar Technologies

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.500
and NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory,

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.740
will carry a payload of
scientific instruments.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.000
The instruments will determine

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.070
if Psyche has a magnetic field,

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.770
study its chemical and
mineral composition,

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.080
and map out its topography.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.080
Psyche is currently the only
known place in our solar system

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.380
where scientists can examine
directly what may contain metal

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.540
from the core of a planetesimal.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.250
- NASA seems to be,

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.520
in what some scientists call
the golden age of asteroids.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.800
Asteroids and small bodies like comets

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.150
were ignored for a long time
in lieu of going to the moon

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.610
and trying to figure
out how to get to Mars.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.650
And now I think NASA is really

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.150
putting its money where its mouth is

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.790
in terms of exploring
these types of worlds.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:36.450
And while the most recent
asteroid related mission

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.880
brought back samples
from a different asteroid

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.100
and Psyche isn't bringing back samples,

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.400
the rarity of this metallic world

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.960
and what we could learn from it

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.501
really is what gives this mission value.

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:51.084
(upbeat music)

